            A12: QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec1, mu7, NPrec2, mu8, NPVARrec1.cases); 
                 PREPPrec1 := VARPREPPrec1
          A1: NPrec2.generic := omegageneric;
              NPrec2.superdeixis := omegadeixis;
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec2.generic = omegageneric AND
              NPrec2.superdeixis = omegadeixis
            C11: NPrec2.mood = nowh AND
                 PREPPrec1.mood = nowh
            A11: QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec2, mu8, NPrec1, mu7, []); 
                 NPVARrec1 := COPYT_nptovar(NPrec2);
                 NPVARrec1.mood := topicmood;
                 VARPREPPrec1 := PREPPrec1;
                 VARPREPPrec1.mood := topicmood
            C12: NPrec2.mood = wh AND
                 PREPPrec1.mood = wh
            A12: QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec2, mu8, NPrec1, mu7, []); 
                 NPVARrec1 := COPYT_nptovar(NPrec2);
                 VARPREPPrec1 := PREPPrec1
          A1: QUOTE_assdeixismax(CLAUSErec1.deixis, CLAUSErec1.superdeixis,
                                 NPrec1.superdeixis);
              NPVARrec1.index := LEVEL;
              NPVARrec1.generic := nogeneric;
              NPrec1.generic := nogeneric
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RShiftVarPrepNPSubst
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
shifted prepobjrel: to x1 did you give it $\rightarrow$ to whom did you give 
it\\
shifted byobjrel: by x1 were you hit $\rightarrow$ by whom were you hit
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_Substitution
\item[* date of creation:] 10-OCT-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch Rsubstitution16
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 15/03/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
1) added conditions on absence of BIGPROs (needed for NOC)\\
2) added conditions on absence of an element with incorporated negation, since 
such a word must be broken down to a separate negation (no local translation of 
a word like `nobody' should be possible, except when translating bare NPs)
\item date: 13/11/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Added conditions for topicmood (had been forgotten; only RShiftNPSubst was 
adapted).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to substitute NPs for NPVARs inside shifted VARPREPPs. These 
VARPREPPs 
have been made in the startrules (for prepobjrels) or in the voicerules (for 
byobjrels). 
Since the original relation (prepobjrel, byobjrel) has been lost in 
the shifting, and since the shifted element may have moved to a higher 
sentence, no conditions can be formulated on the synvpefs of the CLAUSE to 
help prevent creation of an ambiguous path (see previous rule, where
shifted dirargrel, locargrel, complrel, predrel/PREPPs have to 
be made on basis of the same input model)
